## Props

A ListGroup of items that may need a look, worst first: `critical`, then `caution`, `neutral` and `positive`. Each row ends in its status as StatusText, and the group shows `empty` when there's nothing to list.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `title` (required) | `React.ReactNode` |  | The list's heading, such as "Needs attention". |
| `summary` | `React.ReactNode` |  | The one-line takeaway beside the heading, such as "2 failed, 1 would change". |
| `items` (required) | `StatusItem[]` |  |  |
| `empty` | `React.ReactNode` |  | Shown in place of the rows when no item is listed. Default “Nothing needs a look.” |
| `subtitleLines` | `1 \| 2 \| 'all'` | `2` | Lines each subtitle shows before it ends in an ellipsis: 1, 2 or `'all'`. Default 2. |
| `headingLevel` | `2 \| 3 \| 4 \| 5 \| 6` | `2` | Heading level for `title`. Default 2. |
| `footer` | `React.ReactNode` |  |  |
| `className` | `string` |  |  |

## Example

The smallest working use, from the docs site:

```tsx
import { StatusList, type StatusItem } from '@/components/lede/blocks/status-list';

export function NeedsAttention({ items }: { items: StatusItem[] }) {
  const failed = items.filter((i) => i.tone === 'critical').length;
  return (
    <StatusList
      title="Needs attention"
      summary={items.length ? `${failed} failed of ${items.length}` : undefined}
      items={items}
      empty="Nothing needs a look. Every host deployed and checked in."
    />
  );
}
```

Docs: [Blocks](https://lede.cloudcompute.com/blocks.md).

